/*!
  \page example_cu_fit_plane_page Fitting in CUDA kernels

  This example fits a plane at every point of a planar point cloud in a CUDA kernel: each thread sets up a fit at the
  position of its point, iterates over all the points of the cloud (stored in device memory), and writes the
  potential and the gradient of the fitted plane. Without spatial data structure, every thread visits every point;
  see \ref example_cu_kdtree_page for a version using a kd-tree.

  To compile and run the example:
  \code{.sh}
  cmake --build build --target cuda_fit_plane
  ./build/examples/cuda/cuda_fit_plane
  \endcode

  See also \ref ponca_gpu_page.

  \include cuda/ponca_fit_plane.cu
 */
